LINEAGE & ACKNOWLEDGMENTS

Fukuii is an independent, ground-up execution client — Ethereum Classic's first
native client built for connectivity to the greater EVM ecosystem. It is written
from scratch, but it stands on a lineage of vision and craft it is proud to name:

  ETCDEV — Orbita (2018)
    Igor Artamonov ("splix") and the ETCDEV team presented Orbita at ETC Summit
    2018 in Seoul: a standardized sidechain framework for Ethereum Classic and an
    early vision of a multi-network client. The Sidekick prototype was never
    finished. Fukuii carries that vision forward — an "orbita" is a chain instance
    within the fukuii runtime.

  IOHK — Mantis
    Input Output (HK) built Mantis, a Scala client for Ethereum Classic, and chose
    the JVM and Scala for the task — then set it down. Fukuii owes Mantis the
    inspiration for its tech stack. "Mantis" is a trademark of IOHK, named here
    only for that inspiration and this project's origin story.

  Chippr Robotics LLC and White B0x Inc. — Fukuii
    The Fukuii developers, who realized the dream: Ethereum Classic's first native
    client with a bridge to the wider EVM world.

  -- the story --
    Chordodes fukuii is a nematomorph — a parasitic worm that infects a mantis,
    rewires its nervous system, and drives it toward water, where the worm
    completes its lifecycle. The mantis becomes a vehicle for something else
    entirely. Mantis was abandoned; from it, Fukuii emerged — rebuilt from the
    ground up, wearing the name, driven toward consensus. 🪱🧠

================================================================================

Fukuii is an original, ground-up rewrite. It contains no source code from IOHK's
Mantis client and is not a derivative work of Mantis; it is therefore not subject
to the copyright or license terms of Mantis. The Mantis and Orbita names are
acknowledged above for lineage and inspiration only.

